body:

<div id="page-body-countdown-container"></div>

<img src="/current/starship-pad-boat.jpg" alt="Photo of the SpaceX Starship on the pad, with a boat in the foreground" style="display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; margin-top: 5px; margin-bottom: 20px;">

Join Star Fleet for the first-ever flight attempt of a fully-reusable orbital rocket, the "holy grail" of rocketry, and the first ever landing attempt of both the Starship upper stage and the V3 version of the Super Heavy booster!
The launch is ** *No Earlier Than* Friday November 13 at 4:45 PM CST (22:45 UTC) **, and we'll be out there to view it!
In addition, we'll run a separate trip at a discount to view the landing, from the very same close-up spot (hazard zones allowing, which are currently to-be-confirmed but should be known before we release tickets for it).

Our planned [Starship launch viewing location at the mouth of the South Bay](https://www.google.com/maps/search/26.052814,+-97.185356), approximately 4 miles / 6.5 km from the launch site with a direct line of sight across the water, provides some of the closest and clearest views of the pad, rocket, liftoff, and booster landing available to the public.
Unlike the location where most other vessels anchor, this offers a closer and clearer sightline, and has calmer, less busy waters without the need to constantly jockey for position.
For ship landing, we plan to be in the mouth of the Brownsville ship channel, with is both nearly as close as possible to the pad while having an ideal view of the Starship on approach as it makes a wide 270 degree turn with our location essentially at the pivot point.


**LATEST LAUNCH UPDATE**:
As of *Friday November 13*, SpaceX continues to target today for launch in a 4:45 PM - 6:00 PM CST (22:45-00:00 UTC) launch window, with good weather forecast for launch and acceptable weather for landing at the moment, although the latter does appear to be a watch item.
Official FAA signoff has not yet been received, but is still expected today.
Looking forward to seeing you all there!

Due to very high demand for this launch, despite booking multiple additional boats we are completely SOLD OUT for launch, with a few ship landing tickets still available!
If you're still looking for a spot for launch, we recommend Fish Tales charters in Port Isabel, located at the foot of the bridge to SPI right near Hopper Haus and the Osprey.
We've worked with them in the past, and they have a similar double-decker boat and should be going to the same location as we do.
To book their boat, contact them at [956-943-3185](tel:+19569433185).

*We have **[a Whats App community](INSERT_URL_1) that we highly recommend you join**, with channels for announcements, insider launch updates, discussion, questions and more!
We also use it for early tickets, special community events and more!
You can also follow our [Twitter](https://twitter.com/StarFleetTours), [Instagram](https://instagram.com/starfleettours/) and [Facebook](https://www.facebook.com/starfleettours/) for announcements and updates.
Thanks!*

